      "description": "One point per trip over 5 km. Expect wide scatter: a short cold trip at low average speed can read three times a steady motorway run, and both are normal. Observed range over the 7.5 weeks to 2026-09-05 was roughly 85 to 355 Wh/km per trip, against about 124 Wh/km net overall.\n\nReading it: a sustained upward shift at similar speeds and temperatures is the interesting signal -- dragging brakes, low tyres, or a genuinely weakening pack.",
